/**
 * DOC-01 — Dr. Yaz Dominguez × Hume Body Pod
 * Doctor advertorial / review-style landing page.
 *
 * Hook: "I thought body-composition scales were useless, until one changed how I coach every patient."
 * Format modeled on the IM8 doctor advertorials (reviews.amymdwellness.com, dr-dawn.co, dr-arasuppiah.com).
 * Source of truth: docs/hume-reference/ (build brief + copy-research brief + master research report).
 *
 * STATUS: Copy drafted in Dr. Yaz's voice (he greenlit this story; final to be shown to him and updated).
 * All imagery is PLACEHOLDER — see <ImgPlaceholder> labels and docs/hume-reference/IMAGE-MANIFEST.md.
 *
 * COMPLIANCE (binding — see docs/hume-reference/brand/research-report.md Part C1):
 *  - Every body metric is an insight / estimate / TREND for general wellness — never diagnosis,
 *    treatment, cure, prevention, or guaranteed outcome. Sensitive metrics paired with a disclaimer.
 *  - Accuracy = "≈98% CORRELATION with DEXA under consistent conditions" / "within ±2–3% (Socotech, third-party)".
 *    Never "98% accurate", "medical-grade", or "replaces your DEXA/doctor".
 *  - GLP-1 named only as the patient's personal context; device only TRACKS. No treatment claims.
 *  - FTC paid-partnership disclosure at the top and beside every CTA (he is a compensated endorser).
 */

